-- title:
--   Every fibre reading is realised on an affine open
-- statement:
--   Let $B_1$ be a local ring with residue field $k =$ `ResidueField B₁`, and let $V$ be a finite-dimensional $k$-vector space which is at the same time a $B_1$-module compatibly with the $k$-structure (the scalar tower $B_1 \to k \to \operatorname{End} V$), equipped with a $B_1$-linear map $\iota : V \to B_1$. Let $f : X \to \operatorname{Spec} B_1$ and $f_k : X_k \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be schemes over the base and its residue field, and let $i : X_k \to X$ be such that the square formed by $i$, $f_k$, $f$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue homomorphism $B_1 \to k$ is cartesian. Let $U \subseteq X$ be an affine open, and $W \subseteq X_k$ an open with $W \le i^{-1}U$ and $i^{-1}U \le W$ (so $W = i^{-1}U$). Finally let $w : V^{\vee} \to \Gamma(X_k, W)$ be $k$-linear, where $V^{\vee} = \operatorname{Hom}_k(V,k)$ and the target is the value at $W$ of the unit $\mathcal{O}$-module presheaf of $f_k$, i.e. the ring of sections with its $k$-module structure. Then there is a section $\delta \in \Gamma(X,U)$, where $\Gamma(X,U)$ is a $B_1$-algebra through $f$, such that $\delta$ lies in the ideal of $\Gamma(X,U)$ generated by the image of the ideal $\iota(V) \subseteq B_1$, and such that `IsFibreReading` holds for $\delta$ and $w$: there are $n \in \mathbb{N}$, vectors $v_1,\dots,v_n \in V$ and sections $s_1,\dots,s_n \in \Gamma(X,U)$ with $\sum_j \iota(v_j)\, s_j = \delta$ (the coefficients taken through the structure map $B_1 \to \Gamma(X,U)$) and $w(\xi) = \sum_j \xi(v_j)\cdot \big(i^{\sharp}_U(s_j)\big)|_W$ for every $\xi \in V^{\vee}$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity step for fibre readings: on an affine open every $k$-linear map $V^{\vee} \to \Gamma(X_k, i^{-1}U)$ arises as the reading along $\iota$ of a section of $X$ over $U$ lying in the ideal generated by $\iota(V)$. It feeds the construction of Čech cocycles for the Picard obstruction of a small extension, being used in the existence results for fibre readings with prescribed cocycle, and in the recognition of invertible pullbacks and of trivialisations of the unit in the deformation-theoretic arguments.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_SmallExtension_exists_mem_map_range_and_isFibreReading_of_isAffineOpen.lean

